eckSlide(slide_number=7, title='Future Consumers Are at Our Door', text='An extensive survey commissioned with the Harris Poll reveals that new consumers desire our products. Key findings: 72% are women, 33% are boomers, 54% do not currently use cannabis, and 63% are interested in edibles.', graph_desc=[\"A woman holding a pink 1906 'LOVE' branded product in her hand, partially obscured by a light-colored bag. The woman is wearing a reddish-brown ribbed top.\"], section='Market Opportunity'), DeckSlide(slide_number=8, title='Functional Cannabis Is Becoming Mainstream', text=\"A recent survey indicates that 3 out of 4 adults are interested in cannabis as medicine. Many people currently rely on pharmaceuticals and alcohol, but prefer plant-based alternatives. Most cannabis users already use it for pain, anxiety, or sleep, not just to 'get high'. Antidepressant use has surged 65% in 15 years. 70% of women experience anxiety monthly. 30-40 million adults have trouble sleeping nightly. 75% of people are interested in cannabis as medicine.\", graph_desc=['No specific graph, but a list of statistics is presented on the right side of the slide.'], section='Market Opportunity'), DeckSlide(slide_number=9, title='1906 Experiences to Enhance and Optimize Your Day and Night', text='1906 offers six distinct experiences: AROUSAL (LOVE - aphrodisiac blend), ENERGY (GO - high-functioning cannabis with caffeine and energizing herbs), RELAXATION (CHILL - stress-reducing plant medicines and relaxing cannabis), EUPHORIA (BLISS - all-natural euphoric high with targeted herbs and specialized cannabis), SLEEP (MIDNIGHT - sleep-promoting herbs and relaxing cannabis), and COGNITIVE FOCUS (GENIUS - plant medicines for attention and mental clarity).', graph_desc=['Six vertical panels, each representing a different 1906 product line (AROUSAL, ENERGY, RELAXATION, EUPHORIA, SLEEP, COGNITIVE FOCUS) with corresponding product packaging (LOVE, GO, CHILL, BLISS, MIDNIGHT, GENIUS) shown at the bottom of each panel.'], section='Products'), DeckSlide(slide_number=10, title='Unique Plant Medicine Formulations', text='We are the only company to incorporate other plant medicines and supplements in our experience-focused formulations. The map highlights the global sourcing of these ingredients: Damiana (Arousal), Catuaba (Arousal), Muira Puama (Arousal), Kanna (Euphoria), Rhodiola (Focus), Corydalis (Sleep), Magnolia (Relaxation), Ashwagandha (Arousal), Alpinia Galanga (Energy), and L-Theanine (Relaxation).', graph_desc=['A world map with various plant medicines and supplements highlighted with their functional benefits (e.g., Damiana for Arousal, Rhodiola for Focus, Corydalis for Sleep).'], section='Differentiation'), DeckSlide(slide_number=11, title='Winning the Category', text='1. Fastest-acting edible on the market with patented lipid microencapsulation technology for onset in 20 minutes or less. 2. Superior taste due to novel technology, artisanal ingredients, and world-class chocolate-making. 3. Targeted experiences surpass other edibles. 4. Wide range of consumption options for high-functioning adults.', graph_desc=['A comparison table showing 1906 against competitors (CODA, DIXIE, KIVA, INCREDIBLES) across criteria like Fast Acting, Low Dose, Targeted Effects, Premium Positioning, Cannabis source, Taste of Cannabis, and Broad Product Line. 1906 consistently shows advantages.'], section='Competitive Advantage'), DeckSlide(slide_number=12, title='A Safe and Pleasurable Toolkit for Modern Living', text='1906 offers a range of products in different formats: Confections (chocolates), Pressed Tablets (pills), and Beverages. These products are designed to be a safe and pleasurable toolkit for modern living.', graph_desc=[\"An array of 1906 products categorized into 'Confections' (chocolate pieces, chocolate-covered balls, a bitten chocolate), 'Pressed Tablets' (colorful pill bottles for BLISS, GO, GENIUS, CHILL, MIDNIGHT, LOVE), and 'Beverages' (cans for CHILL, GO, BLISS).\"], section='Products'), DeckSlide(slide_number=13, title='Enhancement at Your Fingertips', text=\"The 1906 experience is simple: PICK YOUR DESIRED EXPERIENCE (unique psychological and physiological effects), CHOOSE HOW YOU'D LIKE TO PARTAKE (Confections, Pressed Tablets/Mints, Beverages), and ENJOY (controlled-dose, artful shapes, gorgeous packaging, delicious taste).\", graph_desc=[\"A grid layout with three columns: 'PICK YOUR DESIRED EXPERIENCE', 'CHOOSE HOW YOU'D LIKE TO PARTAKE', and 'ENJOY'. Each column has a descriptive text below it.\"], section='User Experience'), DeckSlide(slide_number=14, title='Phenomenal Growth Every Quarter', text='The company has experienced significant growth. Cumulative units sold have shown a steep upward trend since inception. Revenue growth from 2018 to 2019 shows increases of 29%, 55%, and 63% across quarters. Sales per store in 2019 also show a 23% growth.', graph_desc=[\"A line graph titled 'Units Sold (cumulative since inception)' showing a steep upward curve from 2016 to 2019, reaching over 500K units. Two bar charts: 'Revenue Growth - 2018 vs. 2019' showing significant percentage growth quarter-over-quarter, and 'Sales Per Store (Per Quarter in 2019)' indicating growth in sales per store.\"], section='Traction'), DeckSlide(slide_number=15, title='Disciplined and Focused Growth Strategy', text='We are disciplined and focused on how we grow. We are building manufacturing facilities in Illinois, Massachusetts, and Michigan with Ascend. We are pursuing a vertically integrated license in New Jersey and have secured local approvals for our Jersey City facility. These states were chosen strategically based on population demographics, geographic reach, and regulatory climates.', graph_desc=['A map of the United States highlighting states where 1906 is expanding (Illinois, Massachusetts, Michigan, New Jersey, Ohio, Colorado) with market size estimates for 2020 and expansion plans for 2021. States are colored pink, blue, and teal.'], section='Market Expansion'), DeckSlide(slide_number=16, title='A Massively Differentiated Offering', text='1. PLANT POWER: Six thoughtful formulations of powerful adaptogens, herbs, and socially dosed cannabis. 2. RAPID ONSET: Proprietary technology for fastest onset (20 minutes or less). 3. OPTIMAL RATIOS OF CBD TO THC: 1:1 for most products, 5:1 for relaxing formulas. 4. QUALITY FIRST: All products use single-strain, pesticide-free cannabis, triple-tested for consistency. 5. INCREDIBLE FLAVOR: Delicious artisanal chocolates with patented flavor masking technology, no cannabis taste.', graph_desc=[\"A close-up image of a person's face with their eyes covered by their hands, and a small blue pill-like edible resting on their tongue.\"], section='Differentiation'), DeckSlide(slide_number=17, title='Unprecedented Technology + Facilities', text=\"We boast industrial-scale R&D and manufacturing operations. Our ethos is 'Even our Standards are High'. We see growth in contract manufacturing opportunities and global sourcing of plant medicines. In early 2020, we are expanding to Massachusetts, Illinois, Michigan, and Ohio, markets primed for low-dose brands like 1906.\", graph_desc=['Two images showing manufacturing facilities. The left image shows a person in protective gear working with machinery. The right image shows another person in protective gear overseeing a production line of small chocolate pieces.'], section='Operations'), DeckSlide(slide_number=18, title='Disruption Is Everything', text=\"Our marketing strategy disrupts the category with a unique brand proposition: Functional Cannabis for high-functioning adults. We enhance daily lives by combining cutting-edge technology with long-proven adaptogens, herbs, and cannabis. Our marketing pillars include Budtender engagement, PR/Media, Social/Influencers, and Experiences. We've gained significant media recognition from outlets like CNN, Vanity Fair, Business Insider, and Vogue, being called 'one of the most innovative new brands in the cannabis sector'.\", graph_desc=['A collage of logos from various media outlets: Cosmopolitan, Bloomberg, POPSUGAR, HIGH TIMES, Forbes, PENTHOUSE, TRENDHUNTER, VOGUE, .Mic, BUSINESS INSIDER, Bloomberg Businessweek, ROOSTER, EATER, The Daily Meal, goop.'], section='Marketing Strategy'), DeckSlide(slide_number=19, title='Customer Testimonials', text=\"Customers praise 1906 products: 'Pure, unadulterated eight hours of sleep, just like the doctor ordered... Midnight chocolates taste fan-friggin-delicious...I would buy 1906 Midnight again in a heartbeat.' (DGO MAGAZINE). '1906's goal is to provide consumers with cannabis products that fit into their daily routine without overpowering them. Midnight contains a highly targeted blend of sleep-inducing plant medicines and relaxing cannabis to promote deeper and more restful sleep.' (MG MAGAZINE). '1906's Love gives you the perfect high for getting it on: body and mind.' (VENNA).\", graph_desc=['Three speech bubble-like text boxes containing positive testimonials about 1906 products (Midnight and Love) from DGO Magazine, MG Magazine, and VENNA.'], section='Testimonials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=20, title='Financial Forecasts ($ Millions)', text='The financial forecasts show significant revenue growth from 2017 to 2021, with total revenue projected to reach $52.75 million in 2021 under the stretch case. Gross margin is expected to increase from 45% in 2017 to 58% in 2021. EBITDA is projected to turn positive in 2020 under the stretch case and reach $20.38 million in 2021.', graph_desc=['A table displaying financial forecasts in millions of dollars from 2017 to 2021, including Total Revenue, revenue breakdown by state and product, COGS, Gross Margin, Total Expenses, and EBITDA, with Base Case and Stretch Case scenarios for 2020 and 2021.'], section='Financials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=21, title='Contract Manufacturing Partnerships', text=\"Other brands are tapping into our skills for contract manufacturing. This slide highlights partnerships with 'Willie's Reserve' and 'Beboe', showcasing our capabilities in producing cannabis products for other companies.\", graph_desc=[\"The logo for 'WILLIE'S RESERVE' on the left. On the right, various product packaging for 'BEBOE' branded cannabis products, including boxes and a circular tin.\"], section='Partnerships'), DeckSlide(slide_number=22, title='Disciplined Rollout Over the Next 18 Months', text='We plan a disciplined rollout to increase access to our products. In Q3 2019, we launched Pressed Tablets & Genius Experience. Q4 2019 saw Gummies Launch. Q1 2020 included Illinois Launch. Q2 2020 brought Massachusetts Launch. Q3 2020 will feature 1906 Retail Experience (Boston), Beverages, and Michigan Launch. Q4 2020 will see Ohio Launch, and Q1 2021 will include New Jersey Launch. Note: The launch of vapes is on hold due to the current vaping crisis.', graph_desc=['A timeline chart illustrating the rollout plan for 1906 products and market expansion from Q3 2019 to Q1 2021, including launches for Pressed Tablets & Genius Experience, Gummies, Beverages, and state launches in Illinois, Massachusetts, Michigan, Ohio, and New Jersey.'], section='Roadmap'), DeckSlide(slide_number=23, title='A World-Class Team of Visionaries (Part 1)', text='The team includes: PETER BARSOOM (CEO & Co-founder) with extensive finance and business strategy experience. ERIN HOLZER (Operations & Manufacturing) with 11+ years in chocolate manufacturing, former Chief Chocolate Maker at Theo Chocolate, built a factory capable of 4M pounds of products. JACKIE CORNELL (Chief of Policy & Health Innovations), former Principal Deputy Commissioner of NJ Health Department. HEATHER LARIMER (Chief Marketing Officer), writer and creative director for top brands like Apple, YouTube, Nike, and focused on brand strategy.', graph_desc=['Headshots and brief bios for Peter Barsoom (CEO & Co-founder), Erin Holzer (Operations & Manufacturing), Jackie Cornell (Chief of Policy & Health Innovations), and Heather Larimer (Chief Marketing Officer).'], section='Team'), DeckSlide(slide_number=24, title='A World-Class Team of Visionaries (Part 2)', text='The team continues with: JIM FREELAND (Director of Sales, Retail & Field Marketing) with 25+ years in wholesale and retail merchandising. JUSTIN KIRKLAND (Science & Technology (Consulting)) with 10+ years in pharmaceutical, botanical, and dietary supplements, patented the first water-soluble certified CBD organic delivery system. LAMIA MCKEARN (Colorado License Holder & Administration) with 20 years in direct importing, former owner/manager of Habitat Imports, and degrees in Biology and Psychology. NATASHA LANNERD (Director of Business Development) with extensive background in sales management and business development in natural foods and cannabis sectors. LAUREN PETERSEN (Director of Retail Operations), former General Manager of Silverpeak Apothecary.', graph_desc=['Headshots and brief bios for Jim Freeland (Director of Sales, Retail & Field Marketing), Justin Kirkland (Science & Technology (Consulting)), Lamia McKearn (Colorado License Holder & Administration), Natasha Lannerd (Director of Business Development), and Lauren Petersen (Director of Retail Operations).'], section='Team'), DeckSlide(slide_number=25, title='This Is Your Moment', text='This is a massive market opportunity. We are creating a category of premium, experiential products in a market with limited differentiation. We have a team with a vision and proven track record. We offer superior economics and attractive return on investment. Be a part of the fastest-growing piece of the fastest-growing industry. Help create an entirely new category of fast-acting cannabis/plant medicines.', graph_desc=['A grid of six text boxes, each highlighting a key reason to invest or join: Massive market opportunity, Creating a new category, Team with vision and track record, Superior economics, Part of fastest-growing industry, Creating new category of fast-acting cannabis/plant medicines.'], section='Call to Action'), DeckSlide(slide_number=26, title='Appendix: Market Research and Industry Context', text='This slide serves as a divider for the appendix section, indicating that the following slides will provide market research and industry context.', graph_desc=[], section='Appendix'), DeckSlide(slide_number=27, title='1906 Has Created a Brand at the Leading Edge of the Future Cannabis Industry', text='Adult use of cannabis is legal in 10 states, and medical cannabis in 33 states, with 62% of Americans supporting legalization. The cannabis market is experiencing 42% year-over-year growth and is projected to reach $50 billion. Annual U.S. Legal Cannabis Revenue Projections show significant growth from $4.2 billion in 2018 to $22.6 billion in 2021, with both recreational and medical segments contributing.', graph_desc=[\"A bar chart comparing 'Annual U.S. Cannabis Sales vs. Other Industries & Goods' (e.g., Beer, Cigarettes, Video Games, Firearms & Ammunition, McDonald's, Netflix, Organic Produce, Tattoos, Oreos) with legal cannabis sales. A stacked bar chart titled 'U.S. Legal Cannabis Revenue Projections' showing the growth of recreational and medical cannabis revenue from 2018 to 2021.\"], section='Market Overview'), DeckSlide(slide_number=28, title=\"Our Research Tells Us We're Exactly What Consumers Need\", text=\"A Harris Poll partnership revealed that consumers want the dispensary experience to change to meet their needs. Most people don't want to get high; they want to be well. They seek cannabis for specific benefits and prefer non-smokable alternatives. 1906 is built on these insights. 79% want to relax, 72% want to relieve pain, 68% want help with sleep, 65% want to relieve anxiety, and only 35% like the feeling of being high.\", graph_desc=['A list of percentages and corresponding consumer desires regarding cannabis use: 79% want to relax, 72% want to relieve pain, 68% want help with sleep, 65% want to relieve anxiety, and 35% like the feeling of being high.'], section='Consumer Insights'), DeckSlide(slide_number=29, title='\"Health\" Trumps High', text=\"The vast majority of consumers are looking to get well, not to get stoned. Testimonials include: 'Allow me to come in and not judge. I use it for pain, not to get high.' (Woman, 42, Colorado). 'Make me feel reassured that I am doing this for quality of life and not to get high.' (Man, 49, California). 'Provide more options for people who are looking for anxiety help, not to get high.' (Woman, 36, Colorado).\", graph_desc=['Three speech bubble-like text boxes containing quotes from consumers emphasizing health benefits over getting high.'], section='Consumer Insights'), DeckSlide(slide_number=30, title='Our Audience Is Developing Right In Front of Us', text='The emerging audience consists of casual cannabis users and non-users, life hackers interested in optimal living, and a growing presence of women. Our users span a broad age range, have discretionary income, are health-conscious, open-minded, and prefer natural alternatives. They are culturally astute and on the leading edge. 1906 appeals to an upscale, high-functioning demographic (Lululemon, REI, Whole Foods crowd). This lucrative segment will soon substitute 1906 products for alcohol, pharmaceuticals, and energy drinks.', graph_desc=['A stack of three rectangular chocolate-like edibles with small, round, dark brown pieces on top, suggesting a product or ingredient.'], section='Target Audience'), DeckSlide(slide_number=31, title='2020 Sources of Revenue', text='In 2020, 90.0% of revenue came from the 1906 brand, with 10.0% from Beboe. By state, Colorado accounted for 37.4% of revenue, Massachusetts for 36.9%, Michigan for 13.1%, Illinois for 12.0%, and Ohio for 0.6%.', graph_desc=[\"Two pie charts: '2020 Sources of Revenue by Brand' showing 90.0% from 1906 and 10.0% from BEBOE. '2020 Sources of Revenue by State' showing revenue distribution among Colorado (37.4%), Massachusetts (36.9%), Michigan (13.1%), Illinois (12.0%), and Ohio (0.6%).\"], section='Financials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=32, title='Contact Information', text=\"For more information, please contact Peter Barsoom at 917.597.2438 or pbarsoom@nukafoods.com. The company's social media handle is @1906NEWHIGHS and website is 1906NEWHIGHS.COM.\", graph_desc=['An artistic arrangement of small, colorful, cube-shaped objects with chocolate pieces on top, set against a white background.'], section='Contact')]\n",
      "[DeckSlide(slide_number=1, title='Introducing Functional Cannabis', text=\"The slide features the company logo '1906' prominently at the top, centered within a circle. Below the logo, the main title 'Introducing Functional Cannabis' is displayed.\", graph_desc=[], section='Title'), DeckSlide(slide_number=2, title='1906 Product Range', text=\"This slide showcases a variety of 1906 cannabis-infused products, including chocolates and small, colorful pill-like containers. The products are branded with names like 'LOVE', 'MIDNIGHT', 'GO', 'CHILL', 'GENIUS', and 'BLISS', suggesting different functional effects. The items are scattered across a light pink background, with some loose chocolate pieces.\", graph_desc=['An assortment of 1906 branded cannabis products, including chocolate bars, small colorful pill containers, and round tins, with names like LOVE, MIDNIGHT, GO, CHILL, GENIUS, and BLISS.'], section='Products'), DeckSlide(slide_number=3, title='Cannabis and Smoking Are on a Collision Course', text=\"Since legal cannabis began, product options and customer service have focused on smokables. However, carcinogens and lung damage are a concern. The majority of consumers don't want to 'get high' but rather use cannabis for specific conditions. As legalization expands, there's a growing demand for non-smokable, socially dosed, and discreet formats.\", graph_desc=['A close-up photograph of a cannabis plant with purple and green hues, illuminated by a pinkish-orange light.'], section='Problem'), DeckSlide(slide_number=4, title='Edibles Are the Future', text='The edibles category has been problematic due to cheaply made, unpredictable, and bad-tasting products. Most edibles lack specific therapeutic effects and have a slow activation time, leading to negative experiences. Consumers need healthier, more effective options that meet their specific needs.', graph_desc=[\"A close-up image of a person's mouth with red lipstick, holding a small, round, dark brown edible between their lips.\"], section='Problem'), DeckSlide(slide_number=5, title='Solving the Problem with Edibles Opens Up a Whole New World', text=\"Our company is pioneering non-smokable, controlled doses of cannabis and plant medicines in safe, discreet, and user-friendly formats. This approach enables cannabis to function as a wellness tool and a performance-enhancing 'supplement'. Our products: 1. Taste great, 2. Deliver specific effects, and 3. Activate in record time.\", graph_desc=[\"A person lying down, with another person's hands gently covering their eyes, while a small blue pill-like edible is placed on the lower lip of the person lying down. Another blue edible is visible on the forehead of the person whose eyes are covered.\"], section='Solution'), DeckSlide(slide_number=6, title='Meet Functional Cannabis', text=\"The current cannabis market caters to 'stoners'. There's a large, untapped segment of health and wellness-focused individuals who haven't yet discovered cannabis as a self-care tool. 1906 bridges the cannabis and wellness markets by creating finely tuned formulas that enhance key aspects of high-functioning adults' lives: sleep, sex, energy, cognitive focus, relaxation, and mood.\", graph_desc=['A close-up of a hand holding a small, light-colored pill-like edible, with a person wearing yellow pants in the background.'], section='Solution'), DeckSlide(slide_number=7, title='Future Consumers Are at Our Door', text='An extensive survey commissioned with the Harris Poll reveals that new consumers desire our products. Key findings: 72% are women, 33% are boomers, 54% do not currently use cannabis, and 63% are interested in edibles.', graph_desc=[\"A woman holding a pink 1906 'LOVE' branded product in her hand, partially obscured by a light-colored bag. The woman is wearing a reddish-brown ribbed top.\"], section='Market Opportunity'), DeckSlide(slide_number=8, title='Functional Cannabis Is Becoming Mainstream', text=\"A recent survey indicates that 3 out of 4 adults are interested in cannabis as medicine. Many people currently rely on pharmaceuticals and alcohol, but prefer plant-based alternatives. Most cannabis users already use it for pain, anxiety, or sleep, not just to 'get high'. Antidepressant use has surged 65% in 15 years. 70% of women experience anxiety monthly. 30-40 million adults have trouble sleeping nightly. 75% of people are interested in cannabis as medicine.\", graph_desc=['No specific graph, but a list of statistics is presented on the right side of the slide.'], section='Market Opportunity'), DeckSlide(slide_number=9, title='1906 Experiences to Enhance and Optimize Your Day and Night', text='1906 offers six distinct experiences: AROUSAL (LOVE - aphrodisiac blend), ENERGY (GO - high-functioning cannabis with caffeine and energizing herbs), RELAXATION (CHILL - stress-reducing plant medicines and relaxing cannabis), EUPHORIA (BLISS - all-natural euphoric high with targeted herbs and specialized cannabis), SLEEP (MIDNIGHT - sleep-promoting herbs and relaxing cannabis), and COGNITIVE FOCUS (GENIUS - plant medicines for attention and mental clarity).', graph_desc=['Six vertical panels, each representing a different 1906 product line (AROUSAL, ENERGY, RELAXATION, EUPHORIA, SLEEP, COGNITIVE FOCUS) with corresponding product packaging (LOVE, GO, CHILL, BLISS, MIDNIGHT, GENIUS) shown at the bottom of each panel.'], section='Products'), DeckSlide(slide_number=10, title='Unique Plant Medicine Formulations', text='We are the only company to incorporate other plant medicines and supplements in our experience-focused formulations. The map highlights the global sourcing of these ingredients: Damiana (Arousal), Catuaba (Arousal), Muira Puama (Arousal), Kanna (Euphoria), Rhodiola (Focus), Corydalis (Sleep), Magnolia (Relaxation), Ashwagandha (Arousal), Alpinia Galanga (Energy), and L-Theanine (Relaxation).', graph_desc=['A world map with various plant medicines and supplements highlighted with their functional b