 close-up image of a person's face with their eyes covered by their hands, and a small blue pill-like edible resting on their tongue.\"], section='Differentiation'), DeckSlide(slide_number=17, title='Unprecedented Technology + Facilities', text=\"We boast industrial-scale R&D and manufacturing operations. Our ethos is 'Even our Standards are High'. We see growth in contract manufacturing opportunities and global sourcing of plant medicines. In early 2020, we are expanding to Massachusetts, Illinois, Michigan, and Ohio, markets primed for low-dose brands like 1906.\", graph_desc=['Two images showing manufacturing facilities. The left image shows a person in protective gear working with machinery. The right image shows another person in protective gear overseeing a production line of small chocolate pieces.'], section='Operations'), DeckSlide(slide_number=18, title='Disruption Is Everything', text=\"Our marketing strategy disrupts the category with a unique brand proposition: Functional Cannabis for high-functioning adults. We enhance daily lives by combining cutting-edge technology with long-proven adaptogens, herbs, and cannabis. Our marketing pillars include Budtender engagement, PR/Media, Social/Influencers, and Experiences. We've gained significant media recognition from outlets like CNN, Vanity Fair, Business Insider, and Vogue, being called 'one of the most innovative new brands in the cannabis sector'.\", graph_desc=['A collage of logos from various media outlets: Cosmopolitan, Bloomberg, POPSUGAR, HIGH TIMES, Forbes, PENTHOUSE, TRENDHUNTER, VOGUE, .Mic, BUSINESS INSIDER, Bloomberg Businessweek, ROOSTER, EATER, The Daily Meal, goop.'], section='Marketing Strategy'), DeckSlide(slide_number=19, title='Customer Testimonials', text=\"Customers praise 1906 products: 'Pure, unadulterated eight hours of sleep, just like the doctor ordered... Midnight chocolates taste fan-friggin-delicious...I would buy 1906 Midnight again in a heartbeat.' (DGO MAGAZINE). '1906's goal is to provide consumers with cannabis products that fit into their daily routine without overpowering them. Midnight contains a highly targeted blend of sleep-inducing plant medicines and relaxing cannabis to promote deeper and more restful sleep.' (MG MAGAZINE). '1906's Love gives you the perfect high for getting it on: body and mind.' (VENNA).\", graph_desc=['Three speech bubble-like text boxes containing positive testimonials about 1906 products (Midnight and Love) from DGO Magazine, MG Magazine, and VENNA.'], section='Testimonials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=20, title='Financial Forecasts ($ Millions)', text='The financial forecasts show significant revenue growth from 2017 to 2021, with total revenue projected to reach $52.75 million in 2021 under the stretch case. Gross margin is expected to increase from 45% in 2017 to 58% in 2021. EBITDA is projected to turn positive in 2020 under the stretch case and reach $20.38 million in 2021.', graph_desc=['A table displaying financial forecasts in millions of dollars from 2017 to 2021, including Total Revenue, revenue breakdown by state and product, COGS, Gross Margin, Total Expenses, and EBITDA, with Base Case and Stretch Case scenarios for 2020 and 2021.'], section='Financials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=21, title='Contract Manufacturing Partnerships', text=\"Other brands are tapping into our skills for contract manufacturing. This slide highlights partnerships with 'Willie's Reserve' and 'Beboe', showcasing our capabilities in producing cannabis products for other companies.\", graph_desc=[\"The logo for 'WILLIE'S RESERVE' on the left. On the right, various product packaging for 'BEBOE' branded cannabis products, including boxes and a circular tin.\"], section='Partnerships'), DeckSlide(slide_number=22, title='Disciplined Rollout Over the Next 18 Months', text='We plan a disciplined rollout to increase access to our products. In Q3 2019, we launched Pressed Tablets & Genius Experience. Q4 2019 saw Gummies Launch. Q1 2020 included Illinois Launch. Q2 2020 brought Massachusetts Launch. Q3 2020 will feature 1906 Retail Experience (Boston), Beverages, and Michigan Launch. Q4 2020 will see Ohio Launch, and Q1 2021 will include New Jersey Launch. Note: The launch of vapes is on hold due to the current vaping crisis.', graph_desc=['A timeline chart illustrating the rollout plan for 1906 products and market expansion from Q3 2019 to Q1 2021, including launches for Pressed Tablets & Genius Experience, Gummies, Beverages, and state launches in Illinois, Massachusetts, Michigan, Ohio, and New Jersey.'], section='Roadmap'), DeckSlide(slide_number=23, title='A World-Class Team of Visionaries (Part 1)', text='The team includes: PETER BARSOOM (CEO & Co-founder) with extensive finance and business strategy experience. ERIN HOLZER (Operations & Manufacturing) with 11+ years in chocolate manufacturing, former Chief Chocolate Maker at Theo Chocolate, built a factory capable of 4M pounds of products. JACKIE CORNELL (Chief of Policy & Health Innovations), former Principal Deputy Commissioner of NJ Health Department. HEATHER LARIMER (Chief Marketing Officer), writer and creative director for top brands like Apple, YouTube, Nike, and focused on brand strategy.', graph_desc=['Headshots and brief bios for Peter Barsoom (CEO & Co-founder), Erin Holzer (Operations & Manufacturing), Jackie Cornell (Chief of Policy & Health Innovations), and Heather Larimer (Chief Marketing Officer).'], section='Team'), DeckSlide(slide_number=24, title='A World-Class Team of Visionaries (Part 2)', text='The team continues with: JIM FREELAND (Director of Sales, Retail & Field Marketing) with 25+ years in wholesale and retail merchandising. JUSTIN KIRKLAND (Science & Technology (Consulting)) with 10+ years in pharmaceutical, botanical, and dietary supplements, patented the first water-soluble certified CBD organic delivery system. LAMIA MCKEARN (Colorado License Holder & Administration) with 20 years in direct importing, former owner/manager of Habitat Imports, and degrees in Biology and Psychology. NATASHA LANNERD (Director of Business Development) with extensive background in sales management and business development in natural foods and cannabis sectors. LAUREN PETERSEN (Director of Retail Operations), former General Manager of Silverpeak Apothecary.', graph_desc=['Headshots and brief bios for Jim Freeland (Director of Sales, Retail & Field Marketing), Justin Kirkland (Science & Technology (Consulting)), Lamia McKearn (Colorado License Holder & Administration), Natasha Lannerd (Director of Business Development), and Lauren Petersen (Director of Retail Operations).'], section='Team'), DeckSlide(slide_number=25, title='This Is Your Moment', text='This is a massive market opportunity. We are creating a category of premium, experiential products in a market with limited differentiation. We have a team with a vision and proven track record. We offer superior economics and attractive return on investment. Be a part of the fastest-growing piece of the fastest-growing industry. Help create an entirely new category of fast-acting cannabis/plant medicines.', graph_desc=['A grid of six text boxes, each highlighting a key reason to invest or join: Massive market opportunity, Creating a new category, Team with vision and track record, Superior economics, Part of fastest-growing industry, Creating new category of fast-acting cannabis/plant medicines.'], section='Call to Action'), DeckSlide(slide_number=26, title='Appendix: Market Research and Industry Context', text='This slide serves as a divider for the appendix section, indicating that the following slides will provide market research and industry context.', graph_desc=[], section='Appendix'), DeckSlide(slide_number=27, title='1906 Has Created a Brand at the Leading Edge of the Future Cannabis Industry', text='Adult use of cannabis is legal in 10 states, and medical cannabis in 33 states, with 62% of Americans supporting legalization. The cannabis market is experiencing 42% year-over-year growth and is projected to reach $50 billion. Annual U.S. Legal Cannabis Revenue Projections show significant growth from $4.2 billion in 2018 to $22.6 billion in 2021, with both recreational and medical segments contributing.', graph_desc=[\"A bar chart comparing 'Annual U.S. Cannabis Sales vs. Other Industries & Goods' (e.g., Beer, Cigarettes, Video Games, Firearms & Ammunition, McDonald's, Netflix, Organic Produce, Tattoos, Oreos) with legal cannabis sales. A stacked bar chart titled 'U.S. Legal Cannabis Revenue Projections' showing the growth of recreational and medical cannabis revenue from 2018 to 2021.\"], section='Market Overview'), DeckSlide(slide_number=28, title=\"Our Research Tells Us We're Exactly What Consumers Need\", text=\"A Harris Poll partnership revealed that consumers want the dispensary experience to change to meet their needs. Most people don't want to get high; they want to be well. They seek cannabis for specific benefits and prefer non-smokable alternatives. 1906 is built on these insights. 79% want to relax, 72% want to relieve pain, 68% want help with sleep, 65% want to relieve anxiety, and only 35% like the feeling of being high.\", graph_desc=['A list of percentages and corresponding consumer desires regarding cannabis use: 79% want to relax, 72% want to relieve pain, 68% want help with sleep, 65% want to relieve anxiety, and 35% like the feeling of being high.'], section='Consumer Insights'), DeckSlide(slide_number=29, title='\"Health\" Trumps High', text=\"The vast majority of consumers are looking to get well, not to get stoned. Testimonials include: 'Allow me to come in and not judge. I use it for pain, not to get high.' (Woman, 42, Colorado). 'Make me feel reassured that I am doing this for quality of life and not to get high.' (Man, 49, California). 'Provide more options for people who are looking for anxiety help, not to get high.' (Woman, 36, Colorado).\", graph_desc=['Three speech bubble-like text boxes containing quotes from consumers emphasizing health benefits over getting high.'], section='Consumer Insights'), DeckSlide(slide_number=30, title='Our Audience Is Developing Right In Front of Us', text='The emerging audience consists of casual cannabis users and non-users, life hackers interested in optimal living, and a growing presence of women. Our users span a broad age range, have discretionary income, are health-conscious, open-minded, and prefer natural alternatives. They are culturally astute and on the leading edge. 1906 appeals to an upscale, high-functioning demographic (Lululemon, REI, Whole Foods crowd). This lucrative segment will soon substitute 1906 products for alcohol, pharmaceuticals, and energy drinks.', graph_desc=['A stack of three rectangular chocolate-like edibles with small, round, dark brown pieces on top, suggesting a product or ingredient.'], section='Target Audience'), DeckSlide(slide_number=31, title='2020 Sources of Revenue', text='In 2020, 90.0% of revenue came from the 1906 brand, with 10.0% from Beboe. By state, Colorado accounted for 37.4% of revenue, Massachusetts for 36.9%, Michigan for 13.1%, Illinois for 12.0%, and Ohio for 0.6%.', graph_desc=[\"Two pie charts: '2020 Sources of Revenue by Brand' showing 90.0% from 1906 and 10.0% from BEBOE. '2020 Sources of Revenue by State' showing revenue distribution among Colorado (37.4%), Massachusetts (36.9%), Michigan (13.1%), Illinois (12.0%), and Ohio (0.6%).\"], section='Financials'), DeckSlide(slide_number=32, title='Contact Information', text=\"For more information, please contact Peter Barsoom at 917.597.2438 or pbarsoom@nukafoods.com. The company's social media handle is @1906NEWHIGHS and website is 1906NEWHIGHS.COM.\", graph_desc=['An artistic arrangement of small, colorful, cube-shaped objects with chocolate pieces on top, set against a white background.'], section='Contact')]\n",
